To discover available channels, user info, or anything else about the Slack workspace, use the Slack SDK directly:

```python
/Users/luo/Projects/cc-slack-bot/venv/bin/python -c &quot;
from slack_sdk import WebClient
import os
from dotenv import load_dotenv
load_dotenv(&#x27;/Users/luo/Projects/cc-slack-bot/.env&#x27;)
client = WebClient(token=os.environ[&#x27;SLACK_BOT_TOKEN&#x27;])

# List channels
for ch in client.conversations_list(types=&#x27;public_channel,private_channel&#x27;, limit=100)[&#x27;channels&#x27;]:
    print(f&#x27;{ch[\&quot;id\&quot;]} - #{ch[\&quot;name\&quot;]}&#x27;)
&quot;
```

You can call any Slack SDK method this way — list users, read message history, check who&#x27;s online, etc.

